Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:06:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] fix(media): pass the NVENC probe graph inline

FFmpeg 8-era builds removed -filter_complex_script, so the realistic probe
failed with "Unrecognized option" and every render silently fell back to
libx264. Production renders already pass the graph inline; the probe now
does the same. The probe also validated its output after the temporary
directory had been deleted, which made a real ffprobe fail even when the
NVENC encode succeeded; validation now runs before cleanup.

The fake shim identifies the probe by its nvenc_probe.mp4 output name
instead of the removed option. On Windows, where CreateProcess only
resolves .exe, it installs distlib launchers when pip is available so the
shim tests exercise the shim rather than the real ffmpeg.

Attribution: OpenCode (DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free), lane-b/render-basics.
